{{Term/Store|Golden Sparrow|Golden Sparrows|Series, BotW, TotK|plural}} are recurring [[Creature]]s in {{TLoZ Series}}.<ref>{{Cite|'''Golden Sparrow'''|Hyrule Compendium|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|'''Golden Sparrow'''|Hyrule Compendium|TotK}}</ref>

==Characteristics==
==={{BotW|-}}===
{{Compendium/Extract|Golden Sparrow}}
Golden Sparrows are a variety of [[Sparrow]] that inhabit the mountains of the [[Eldin (Region)|Eldin]] [[Region]], primarily the slopes of [[Death Mountain]] itself.<ref>{{Cite Book|quote= |book= CaC |publisher= |page= 164}}</ref><ref name="Compendium">{{Cite|This breed of sparrow is native to the Eldin region. Their down is resistant to burning, an evolutionary trait produced by the harsh volcanic environment. They subsist on small insects that hide inside rocks.|Hyrule Compendium|BotW}}</ref> They survive in this harsh environment thanks to their body feathers being resistant to burning, which protects them from Death Mountain's [[Scorching Climate]].<ref name="Compendium"/> They are primarily predators in diet, and feed on small [[Insect]]s that they search for among rocks.<ref name="Compendium"/> They gather in flocks, but fly away if disturbed. Golden Sparrows drop a single [[Chickaloo Tree Nut]] when killed.

